meta {
  name: Get Integration Inbound Queue Option Sets
  type: http
  seq: 13
}

get {
  url: {{CRM_URL}}/EntityDefinitions(LogicalName='rpa_integrationinboundqueue')/Attributes(LogicalName='{{picklistAttribute}}')/Microsoft.Dynamics.CRM.{{metadataCast}}?$select=LogicalName&$expand=OptionSet($select=Options)
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  $select: LogicalName
  $expand: OptionSet($select=Options)
}

vars:pre-request {
  picklistAttribute: rpa_processingentity
  metadataCast: PicklistAttributeMetadata
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: false
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Returns the permitted values for the choice fields on
  rpa_integrationinboundqueue. Companion to "Get Integration Inbound Queue
  Entity Definition", which establishes that these fields exist but not what
  may be put in them.
  
  This is a prerequisite for writing any record. A Picklist rejects an
  integer that is not one of its defined options, so the write cannot be
  built without these values, and they cannot be guessed from the field
  names.
  
  Run it once per attribute, changing picklistAttribute in vars:pre-request.
  Read Options[].Value for the integer to send and
  Options[].Label.UserLocalizedLabel.Label for what it means.
  
  h4. rpa_processingresult — confirmed on rpadevv9
  
    927350000  Not Started
    927350001  Failed
    927350002  Success
  
  *927350001 is the value the doc-upload integration writes.* The set
  describes the outcome of an attempt, not what went wrong, so it carries no
  distinction between the four failure conditions. That distinction goes in
  rpa_errordetails, which is agreed with DDTS CRM as the field carrying the
  error details, and which is also the only practical place to record which
  submission failed since the entity has no field for the correlation
  identifier.
  
  h4. rpa_processingstage — confirmed on rpadevv9
  
    927350000  Begin Processing
    927350001  End Processing
    927350002  Not Started
  
  This is a lifecycle position, not a reason. It does not distinguish the
  four failure conditions. The reason and the identity of the failed
  submission both go in rpa_errordetails. End Processing is the plausible value for a terminal
  failure, since processing has stopped, but confirm that reading with DDTS
  CRM rather than inferring it from the label.
  
  h4. rpa_processingentity — confirmed on rpadevv9
  
    927350000  Organization
    927350001  Contact
    927350002  Address
    927350003  Contact Role
    927350004  Customer Query
    927350005  eRLE1
    927350006  FFC
    927350007  Bank Account
  
  *No option describes a document upload or the Single Front Door.* The set
  names the kind of record an inbound integration concerns, and nothing in
  it fits this one. Either DDTS CRM add an option or we agree to reuse an
  existing one. Customer Query and FFC are the nearest candidates and
  neither is obviously right. This is a question for David Aitchison rather
  than a judgement for the implementer: the wrong value files the record
  under the wrong integration, where it may never be found. The field is
  optional on create, so leaving it unset until the answer arrives is
  better than guessing.
  
  h4. statuscode — confirmed on rpadevv9
  
    Value 1  Active    (State 0)
    Value 2  Inactive  (State 1)
  
  This is the default two-option set. There are no triage-specific status
  reasons, so statuscode carries no routing meaning and cannot put a record
  into a status that hides it from triage.
  
  Write 1, or omit the field and let the platform default apply. Do not
  write 2: it pairs with State 1, statecode is not valid for create on this
  entity so the record is created in State 0, and the two would be
  inconsistent.
  
  It follows that triage views must be filtering on something other than
  status, most likely rpa_processingresult being Failed. Worth confirming
  with DDTS CRM, since it determines whether a record the integration
  writes actually reaches anyone.
  
  h4. Per environment
  
  Option set values are solution-deployed and can differ between
  environments. Confirm them wherever the write is enabled rather than
  assuming the rpadevv9 values hold.
}
